    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d839">

                <pb facs="1024" n="900" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg900"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.61334/62</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hartman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 7.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 753</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s telegram No.
                    21, of November 16, 2 p.m., relating to the decision of the President of Ecuador
                    to distribute 66 percent of the three sucre tax on cacao exports equally amongst
                    the three groups of claimants, the group having the largest claim being American
                    creditors, without any provision for an extension of the period of levying the
                    tax beyond December 31, 1925, to cover American claims then remaining unpaid, I
                    have the honor to report as follows:—</p>
                <p>I certainly consider the decision unfair to American claims, and accordingly, in
                    compliance with instructions, I addressed my note <pb facs="1025" n="901"
                        xml:id="pg901"/> No. 446, of November 18, 1921, to the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs, three copies of which I herewith enclose.<anchor n="43"
                        xml:id="d839-f1"/></p>
                <p>Upon receipt of the Minister’s answer, I will promptly inform the Department of
                    its contents.</p>
                <p>I have [etc]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chas S. Hartman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
